      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T14:02:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, onStartJob is called on the main thread. It\u0027s expected that it will return and the real work will happen on a separate thread - that\u0027s what the \"return true\" significes.\n\nThe operation here can run for a while, I don\u0027t want to block the background thread for an extended time (there are checks to make sure that doesn\u0027t happen.)\n\nI\u0027d use a thread pool if one is available, but starting \u0026 stopping a thread seemed reasonable. It\u0027s what I\u0027ve done in other jobs.",
